<title>FRANCE: Consensus on need for strong dollar - BOF's Trichet.</title>
<headline>Consensus on need for strong dollar - BOF's Trichet.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet said on Monday that there was a &quot;fairly wide&quot; consensus among Group of Seven rich nations on the need for a strong dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;The issue of the dollar versus the European currencies is subject to a pretty wide consensus. The overall view in the G7 is that a strong dollar is in everyone's interest,&quot; the head of France's independent central bank said on RTL radio.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
